  "schema": "a5sf-zero-boot-preflight/1",
  "label": "BL-17 surface fix — discovery-first leader declaration; the deny list is computed from the discovered surface",
  "sources": {
    "note": "Same World rows and the same base preset as boot #4. The leader blueprint now writes builtinToolDeny from the ACTUAL discovered surface (040-u6-arc-a.mjs:159-161 discovery -> deny -> create; u6-fs-assembly.mjs mainBlueprintYaml(denyList)). The sentinel \"discovery-first\" is the declared rule; the preflight computes the same list with the SAME classifier A2C-2 uses, so the declaration cannot silently rot when the World adds a row. captureLimits.body.maxChars=null on every fail-capable body capture: the boot-4 400/300-char slice is refused by declaration. The plan also declares the discovery step: `discover-leader-surface` produces `leader-surface` and `create-team` requires it, so `driver.gate-order` refuses a driver that creates before it discovers.",
    "computedDenyList": "bash edit read read_image write team_delegate team_archive_member excluded as managed/team; u5_canary and u6fs_probe are the only fatal names -> builtinToolDeny = [u5_canary, u6fs_probe]"
  },
